The same machine that refuses bare reports normally once `--target` names the artifact: the resolved
path is echoed as the `artifact:` and the frontier comes from that file's status.

-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/playbook.md --
---
name: fx-targetless
title: Targetless
summary: Machine with no declared artifact, addressed by --target.
---

Preamble.
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/playbook.yaml --
state: main
graph:
  review: []

states:
  main:
    initial: reviewing
    statuses:
      reviewing:
        transitions:
          - to: reviewed
            when: the review is written
      reviewed: {terminal: true}
-- fixtures/home/Claude/_playbooks/fx-targetless/review/prompt.md --
---
summary: Review the work.
---

Review body.
-- fixtures/cwd/run/review.md --
---
status: reviewing
---

Body.
-- cmd --
booping playbook-state fx-targetless --workdir run --target review.md
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
playbook: fx-targetless
workdir: {CWD}/run
states:
  main:
    artifact: {CWD}/run/review.md
    status: reviewing
    next:
    - to: reviewed
      when: the review is written
